    "description": {
      "value": "You rapidly draw the air from your surroundings, hoarding it for yourself. Creatures in the area when the spell is cast take 5d6 bludgeoning damage with a basic Fortitude save. A creature that fails its save can't speak above a raspy whisper for 1 round. A creature that critically fails can't speak or use abilities that require it to breathe for 1 round. This prevents it from using effects that require speech, such as casting spells with verbal components, and from using a breath weapon or similar ability.\n\nCreatures made of air (such as air elementals) attempting a save against this spell get a degree of success one worse than they rolled."
    },
    "higher_level_description": {
      "value": "Heightened (+1): Increase the damage by 2d6."
    },
